course: dictionary
lesson: 13795
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. The word inventory is a good example. Its main meaning is a complete list of all the things in a place, such as the goods in a shop or the items in a house.
explain: «The shopkeeper took an inventory of every tin on the shelves.» Here inventory is the list of what the shop has. Took an inventory is an action too: it means making a full list. As a verb, to inventory means to make a full list of things, so «She inventoried the toys» means she counted and listed them all.
explain: In a video game, your inventory is the box or list of tools and treasure that your player carries. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning you need. If the words are about counting or listing, think about lists. If the words are about a game and a player, think about what the player carries.
fact: Inventory means a complete list of all the things in a place.
fact: In a shop, inventory means all the goods the shop has ready to sell, which is also called stock.
fact: In a video game, your inventory holds the tools and treasure your player carries.
fact: Useful phrases are take inventory, inventory list and in the inventory.
fact: As a verb, to inventory means to make a full list of things; it is mostly used in American English.
exercise: «The shopkeeper counted every tin and wrote the total on the inventory.» What is the inventory here? | A type of shop window | A cold drink on the counter | A small bag for carrying money | *A complete list of all the things in the shop
exercise: Maya says, «In my game, my inventory is full of swords and potions.» What does inventory mean here? | *The list or box of things a player carries | A score for points | A map of the game world | A shop that sells games
exercise: «Before the move, Dad will inventory every box in the garage.» Which word in this sentence means to make a full list? | *inventory | move | garage | before
test: «After the storm, the sailors made an inventory of the food left on the boat.» What does inventory mean? | A big storm | *A complete list of everything left | A type of boat | A song the sailors sang
test: A shop's goods that are ready to sell are called its stock. Which word means the same as stock? | Discount | Customers | Receipt | *Inventory
exam: «Tom made an inventory of his backpack before the trip.» What does inventory mean in this sentence? | A type of game | A kind of bag | A trip to the shops | *A full list of all the things he has
